      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That's double the usual maximum.\n\n- **Daily maximum:** The FDA-labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day. Extended-release is capped at 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 1,700 mg is well above the usual maximum of 850 to 1,000 mg per dose.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max for IR)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg PO twice daily**, if you're starting metformin and plan to titrate up\n\nIf 1,700 mg/day was the intent, for example 850 mg twice daily, tell me and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and add a note with your rationale. I'd rather not enter it without that."
      }
     ],
