     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I know you've confirmed it. But 5,100 mg/day is twice the labeled maximum, and I don't know of a clinical scenario where it's appropriate. Metformin's glucose-lowering effect plateaus at about 2,000 mg/day, so the extra dose adds toxicity risk without benefit. You also didn't give a rationale for the dose.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- Metformin 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- Metformin 500 mg PO twice daily, then titrate\n\nIf you think this dose is needed, please run it by your attending or the inpatient pharmacist first. If they approve, tell me who and why, and I'll add that to the order note. Otherwise, tell me which option above you want."
      }
     ],
